@startuml
!include ../../../_style.iuml
' Derived from local-ai/room/host.html (onSpeechStart, emitSegment, closeAnswer, gaze loop, status poll),
' local-ai/room/guest.html and room.js (connect, makePeer, handleSignal, getMedia), local-ai/room/__init__.py
' (create_room, transcribe, references, check_answer, answer_similarity, signaling /ws/{room_id}),
' local-ai/room/checks.py (answer_utterances, question_end, signal_list, flag), local-ai/integrity/signals.py
' (DeliveryBaseline, fuse), local-ai/integrity/__init__.py (gaze/frame, status, reading),
' local-ai/room/similarity.py (ReferenceWriter, SimilarityChecker), local-ai/room_server.py (create_room_app).
title OpenMeet Room: one candidate answer from the invite to the integrity flag

hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 260

actor "Interviewer" as IV
participant "host.html\n(interviewer browser)" as HOST
participant "room_server.py\n(FastAPI, this computer)" as SRV
participant "Whisper\n(transcriber)" as W
participant "Echo / reading models,\ngaze tracker" as M
participant "room model\n(Ollama, references)" as R
participant "guest.html\n(candidate browser)" as GUEST
actor "Candidate" as CAND

== Set-up (interviewer computer only) ==

IV -> HOST : opens https://localhost:8443/host
HOST -> SRV : POST /api/rooms (loopback check)
SRV --> HOST : room id, host key, invite links
SRV -> M : monitor.reset() (forget gaze of earlier rooms)
IV -> CAND : sends invite link /join/{room}?k={guest key}
CAND -> GUEST : opens the link, types name, allows camera and microphone
GUEST -> SRV : WSS /ws/{room}?role=guest&k=...&name=...&study_consent (optional)
HOST -> SRV : WSS /ws/{room}?role=host&k=host key (accepted only from loopback)
SRV --> GUEST : hello (peer_present)
SRV --> HOST : peer-joined (name)

== Media: the server only relays the handshake ==

HOST -> SRV : {type: offer, sdp}
SRV -> GUEST : relay offer
GUEST -> SRV : {type: answer, sdp}
SRV -> HOST : relay answer
HOST <--> GUEST : ICE candidates via the server, then WebRTC media (peer to peer)
note over HOST, GUEST
  Video and audio never pass through room_server.py.
  The interviewer's browser sends only speech segments and
  candidate video frames to this computer.
end note

== Gaze, about 10 times a second and once a second ==

loop while connected
  HOST -> HOST : grab a frame of the candidate's video (JPEG)
  HOST -> SRV : POST /v1/integrity/gaze/frame (raw JPEG)
  SRV -> M : add_frame -> iris offset, face found
  HOST -> SRV : GET /v1/integrity/status (about once a second)
  SRV --> HOST : gaze state, live reading probability (if enough gaze)
end

== The candidate speaks (speech cut at pauses) ==

CAND -> HOST : speech (WebRTC audio)
HOST -> HOST : candidate speech starts: answer opens (start time);\nthe question is the interviewer's text since the last answer
HOST -> SRV : POST /api/rooms/{room}/references {question}
SRV -> R : write reference answers to the question (background)
note right of SRV
  Started as soon as the question is heard, so
  the room model is idle again when follow-ups are needed.
end note
HOST -> SRV : POST /api/rooms/{room}/transcribe?speaker=candidate&start&end (WAV)
SRV -> W : transcribe, word timestamps on
W --> SRV : text, words (segment clock + start)
SRV --> HOST : {speaker, start, end, text}
note right of SRV
  Dropped as phantom ("thank you", "bye", ...)
  or when the confidence is below 0.35.
  Kept words land on the meeting clock.
end note

== The answer ends: the interviewer speaks, or presses End answer ==

IV -> HOST : interviewer speaks (or End answer)
HOST -> HOST : closeAnswer: wait for the answer's pending transcriptions
HOST -> SRV : POST /api/rooms/{room}/answers {start, end, text, question, condition?}
SRV -> M : echo: ai_text of the transcript
M --> SRV : probability, level
SRV -> M : reading: gaze series of the answer's window (if 0 < span <= 600 s)
M --> SRV : reading probability, level (or not enough gaze)
SRV -> SRV : delivery: this answer's timings against the candidate's\nfirst answers (checks.py / DeliveryBaseline)
SRV -> SRV : flag = fuse(ai_text, delivery, reading); echo_similarity pending
SRV --> HOST : answer, with flag and signals (similarity pending)

SRV -> R : similarity: cosine of the answer to the reference answers (background)
R --> SRV : highest cosine, level (unavailable unless the spec embedder)
SRV -> SRV : flag recomputed with the four signals
HOST -> SRV : POST /api/rooms/{room}/answers/{index}/similarity (waits for the job)
SRV --> HOST : answer with the final flag

== What the candidate sees ==

note over GUEST
  Nothing about the answer, flag, score or report is sent
  to the candidate's page. The candidate only sees the
  call, its status and the join page statement about
  online or local follow-up questions.
end note
@enduml
